<title>FRANCE: TABLE-French July business outlook improves-INSEE.</title>
<headline>TABLE-French July business outlook improves-INSEE.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-07-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>National statistics institute INSEE gave the following seasonally adjusted data.</p>
<p>A positive figure shows the percentage points by which the percentage of respondents saying things had improved or risen outnumbered the percentage saying things had worsened.</p>
<p>					 July June  May April March  Feb Jan</p>
<p> Recent past output		  13   11    7    6   -3    5   -7</p>
<p> Finished product stocks	   16   17   18   18   21   20   20</p>
<p> Overall orders and demand	-11  -14  -16  -23  -21  -22  -28</p>
<p> Foreign orders and demand	 10   12    3   -6    1    3   -4</p>
<p> Future output (overall)	    3  -12   -7   -3    0    6    1</p>
<p> Future output (personal)	  10   10    5   10   11    9    4</p>
<p> Future prices (overall)	   -7  -11  -12  -12  -13  -11  -13</p>
<p> Future prices (personal)	 -11  -20   -7   -7   -7   -4  -22</p>
<p>RECENT PAST OUTPUT (breakdown)</p>
<p> Manufacturing output		13   11    9    7    2    2  -2</p>
<p> Semi-finished goods		 15   20   11    6    5    0 -10</p>
<p> Industrial capital goods	  18   18   15   14    6    3  14</p>
<p> Cars and land transport	   14  -18  -15    5  -39  -28 -37</p>
<p> Consumer goods			15   13   10    2   -3   -2   0</p>
<p> Agri-food businesses		23   13   12   11   23   26  12</p>
<p> Energy				   -    -    -    -    -    - -86</p>
<p>FUTURE OUTPUT, PERSONAL (breakdown)</p>
<p> Manufacturing output		11   10    7    8    7   13  11</p>
<p> Semi-finished goods		 12   11    9    8    9   13  11</p>
<p> Industrial capital goods	  20   18   20   23   23   15   9</p>
<p> Cars and land transport	  -18    7   12   15  -22   22  19</p>
<p> Consumer goods			 3    4    0    6   10    7   4</p>
<p> Agri-food businesses		19   11   24   17   29   16 -12</p>
<p> Energy				   -    -    -    -    -    - -86</p>
<p>NOTE - INSEE said that for reasons of confidentiality it could not publish energy statistics any later than February.</p>
<p>INSEE also said in the &quot;Future Prices (Personal)&quot; series figures for January, April, July and October should be viewed differently as they are taken from a quarterly survey in which the question asked about prices differs from the monthly survey.</p>
<p>The difference in the way the question is asked means the quarterly figures underestimate price rises or falls, INSEE said.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +331 4221 5452</p>
